<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Choclococha</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Choclococha is a high Andean lake at about 4,600 metres in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huancavelica">Huancavelica</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>. The Chanka regarded it as their pacarina, the sacred place from which their ancestors emerged. It is now part of a reservoir system that diverts water across the Andes to the Ica valley on the coast.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-choclococha.jpg" alt="Lake Choclococha" width="320" height="104" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ibrehaut · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tormenta_llegando_sobre_la_laguna_Choclococha,_en_Jun%C3%ADn,_Per%C3%BA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
